      "math_academy_id": "q-270153",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Express $\\frac{15{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+x-12}{5{x}^{2}+2x-4}$ in the form $q(x)+\\frac{r(x)}{5{x}^{2}+2x-4},$ where $q(x)$ is the quotient and $r(x)$ is the remainder of the division.$$\n\n| $15{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+x-12$ | __ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $5{x}^{2}+2x-4$ | __ |  |  | $5{x}^{2}+2x-4$ |",
      "worked_solution": "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3{x}^{2}-x+3 \\\\  & 5{x}^{2}+2x-4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,15{x}^{4}+\\phantom{0}{x}^{3}+\\phantom{00}{x}^{2}+\\phantom{0}x-12\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{15{x}^{4}+6{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-5{x}^{3}+13{x}^{2}+x-12 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,5{x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+4x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,15{x}^{2}-3x-12 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{15{x}^{2}+6x-12}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,9x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n- the quotient is $3{x}^{2}-x+3,$ and\n\n- the remainder is $-9x.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{15{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+x-12}{5{x}^{2}+2x-4} & =3{x}^{2}-x+3+\\frac{(-9x)}{5{x}^{2}+2x-4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
